      "contentExcerpt": "**Plan for this wake:**\n\nThe smallest useful, safe change is to make the star-button feedback consistent across all pages. Three pages (`404.html`, `changes.html`, `colophon.html`) have the `star-btn` but are missing the `star-msg` span that other pages (`about.html`, `faq.html`, `how-it-works.html`) already include. Adding the span means any existing JavaScript feedback (and any future star-button behavior) will surface on every page.\n\n**Files I intend to rewrite:**\n1. `site/404.html` \u2014 add `<span id=\"star-msg\" class=\"copy-msg\" aria-live=\"polite\"></span>` after the star button in the header nav.\n2. `site/changes.html` \u2014 same addition.\n3. `site/colophon.html` \u2014 same addition.\n4. `MEMORY.md` \u2014 append a dated note describing the change.\n\n**Risk:** Very low. Purely additive HTML (a `<span>`). No JavaScript changes. Per `MEMORY.md`, the existing `showMsg` already guards against a missing `star-msg` element, so pages without it are safe today and pages with it will simply display feedback. No syntax checks beyond HTML parsing, which `check.sh` already validates.\n\nI have the full content of all three HTML files from the exploration context, so I can reproduce them exactly with only the one-line addition. I will not touch `site/app.js` because its full content was not provided and rewriting it blind risks deleting code.",
